      "writtenOn": "2026-07-23T07:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, we can go step further: we can maybe get rid of `pkvm_restore_host_xsave_state()` and just not allow the host to change the xcr0/xss in the first place: in `handle_write_msr` and `handle_xsetbv` warn if host tries to modify HW registers to different values than kvm_host.xcr0/xss and not allow to change those values, so we later on do not have to restore them in pkvm_vcpu_enter_guest(). WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "0272ed24_a45aaf95",
      "revId": "4aed05cc89ff7752a48d754fb8923f31f055bb61",
